{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1334990-query-indefinite-basilisk","id":1334990,"title":"Query: Indefinite Basilisk?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-10T15:44:39-07:00","id":1334990,"title":"Query: Indefinite Basilisk?","content":"Random thought experiment:<br /> <br /> A spell cast with a Basilisk yantra activates on being seen (counting as a single turn duration spell) or fizzles when the spell duration ends. It costs a mana and boosts the duration by two levels.<br /> <br /> Let's say for argument's sake (because this is a thing which very easily can happen) that someone Basilisk-casts a spell with Primary Factor duration and they have enough of the necessary arcana to get an automatic three-step duration increase. They spend a Reach to bump it to Advanced Duration and get it to a 1 month duration without any dice penalties. The bonus two step increase in duration from the Basilisk yantra opens the option to make it Indefinite so they spend the extra Reach and mana to do so.<br /> <br /> At this point the spell will never fizzle. Cool. But does this mean it can Basilisk more than once, or does being seen automatically end the spell? The yantra entry only talks in the context of a spell with a defined duration, not an Indefinite one, so the issue isn't directly addressed.<br /> <br /> Under normal circumstances you could make a small AoE Indefinite duration spell that anchors on an item, and then remove the caster from the potential targets with a bit of additional Prime/Fate (via Dispel Magic with +2 Reaches and a mana to make a Lasting exception). So you can kludge together something vaguely equivalent to an indefinite repeat-activated Basilisk (a business card you tap on someone rather than one they need to look at), but that's slightly more involved to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Yozis are right (and you should suffer and obey for all eternity).</span></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","name":"Zahaqiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T14:58:46-07:00","id":1335198,"title":"","content":"To me, that sounds like it would fire off once unless you use the Imbued Item attainment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-11T18:33:17-07:00","id":1335232,"title":"","content":"That is probably a sensible way of reading it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">The Yozis are right (and you should suffer and obey for all eternity).</span></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1487-zahaqiel","name":"Zahaqiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-02T06:05:39-07:00","id":1338981,"title":"","content":"You forgot the part where it says it only affects a number of people allowed by Scale Factor. So eventually, you would need to recast it. I imagine that Paradox eating your spell over time is also a concern unless you safely relinquished or held onto Spell Control for it.<br /> <br /> Basically this means that the spell will last for the duration set OR until it affects the limit on targets. Whichever comes first.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh and if you're using an AOE anyway, using a Space Key using reach is much safer for creating exceptions. Something like: Key - Not the Caster","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24407,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24407-radriel7","user":"Radriel7","date":". 10-02-2019, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24407-radriel7","name":"Radriel7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24407_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}